We laugh thinking about those first days.
In January, everything here was new.
"Now Kochi is my home," I said.
"Are you going to the flat?"
Sara asked.
"Yes, I am going," I replied.
"Okay Maya, see you next week," Kiran said.
I wave my hand at them.
I walk to the parking area.
My bicycle is there.
I take the key from the bag.
I open the bicycle's lock.
This is a warm April evening.
I ride the bicycle slowly.
Last week I walked along this path.
But today I am on the bicycle.
The roads are very quiet now.
During the trip, I remembered my family.
I reached in front of my flat quickly.
Today was really a good day.
